[13.031756, "o", "   - Extract the count of roles as '\"'\"'role_count'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.031765, "o", "> "]
[13.03203, "o", "   - Extract the first role from the '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' array as '\"'\"'primary_role'\"'\"' (if roles exist, otherwise null).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.032077, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[13.032276, "o", "4. **Sort Users**: Sort the resulting users alphabetically by their '\"'\"'username'\"'\"' in ascending order.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.032304, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.032365, "o", "> "]
[13.032521, "o", "5. **Output Format**: The output must be a JSON array of objects formatted with indentation of 2 spaces.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.032534, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[13.033098, "o", "6. **Save Command**: Save the exact jq command you execute to a file named '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file should contain the complete jq command used to generate the output, including all options and arguments.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[13.033456, "o", "7. **Save Arguments**: Save all jq arguments(excluding input/output files) to a YAML file named '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"'. This file should contain exactly two keys:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
